        {
          "question": "q-333386",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}={e}^{x}-3xy,\\,y(-2)=3\n$$\n\nThe trapezoidal method is applied with step size $\u0394x=1.$ Find the general formula for the new $y$ value, ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ in terms of the current values $x$ and $y,$ and the new value ${x}_{\\text{new}}.$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/state.json",
