          "question": "e-21672",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\ny' = 3x^2 - 2y, \\qquad y(3) = -1\n$$\n\nThe trapezoidal method is applied with step size $\\Delta x = 4.$ Find the general formula for the new $y$ value, $y_\\text{new},$ in terms of the current values $x$ and $y,$ and the new value $x_\\text{new}.$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/example-21672.json",
