    {
      "question": "e-21672",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "70d74bf0d5477ed12f3b42c6a7a9bb2fe443be131e1d8f706087bdcea23cca6a",
      "new_sha256": "0aaf23a4a4544b6f45ffc08e8a7dcf3b91bbbb9c38b4c5d6f75e384d85df16a3",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-21672",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\ny' = f(x,y), \\qquad y(a) = c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $\\Delta x$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\Delta y = \\dfrac12(y' + y'_\\text{new}) \\cdot \\Delta x,\n$$\n\nwith $y'_\\text{new} = f(x_\\text{new}, y_\\text{new})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn this example, $\\Delta y$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u0394y & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{\u2032}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{\u2032})\\cdot \u0394x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(3{x}^{2}-2y+(3({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-2{y}_{\\text{new}}))\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}+6{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-4y-4{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into $y_\\text{new} = y + \\Delta y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\u0394y \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+6{x}^{2}+6{x}_{\\text{new}}^{2}-4y-4{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =6{x}^{2}+6({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-3y-4{y}_{\\text{new}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for the general formula for $y_\\text{new}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{y}_{\\text{new}} & =6{x}^{2}+6({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-3y \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{5}(6{x}^{2}+6({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-3y)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14047192/example-21672.json",
          "file_sha256": "6874e9ab859cf12ba9c4a4d83003ddf5808744c0fc6bc3e9f64f73be41d1985d"
        }
      ],
